AB  - As a core technology of next-generation artificial intelligence, Large Language Models (LLMs) provide breakthrough solutions for the intelligent transformation of power systems. This paper systematically reviews the key technologies, application scenarios, and development prospects of LLMs within the power industry. We particularly emphasize their innovative applications in grid planning, dispatch optimization, equipment operation and maintenance, customer service, and power markets. Utilizing self-attention mechanisms and multimodal learning capabilities, Transformer-based LLMs significantly enhance the efficiency of power grid data parsing, spatiotemporal pattern recognition, and dynamic decision-making. Furthermore, this study explores how language models, vision models, and multimodal models present new opportunities to advance power system intelligence. Finally, the paper highlights the future development of scientific LLMs and their expanding prospects in the power industry, alongside a discussion of implementation challenges, ethical considerations, and future research directions.
